# DESK37 with GEMWIN.NAP -- the minimal GEM program that paints ONLY its own
# window (no v_clrwk, no menu_bar), so what stands behind it is exactly what
# the AES left there. The Hatari counter-picture is
# measurement-2026-09-24-hatari-appbg/screendumps/emutos-bgwin-falcon-tc.png.
#
#   B_WIN1  the C:\ window open
#   C_APP   GEMWIN's window up, the program still running
#   D_APP   the same screen 2 s (400 ticks) later, still running
#
# GEMWIN.NAP holds its window for 6 s = 1200 ticks of the 200 Hz clock the
# injector counts, so both marks sit inside that window (click at +3613).
# They must: the injector is only stepped from the AES input pump, and the
# child's `evnt_timer` wait does not pump, so a mark placed after the 1200
# ticks does not fire late -- it fires once the DESKTOP is back, and would
# photograph the wrong screen (seen once, with marks at +5200/+6200).
#
# Coordinates from d-probe: C: drive icon (38,35); 'GEMWIN.NAP' in window 1
# box (141,171) -> click (179,187).
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 37 42
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
3000 mark B_WIN1
3400 move 179 187
3600 down
3603 up
3610 down
3613 up
3700 move 600 240
4100 mark C_APP
4500 mark D_APP
